Protect Democracy seeks an experienced Director of Finance to head our Finance and Accounting functions, reporting to Executive Leadership. This is an exceptional opportunity for an accomplished financial leader who is passionate about our mission, oriented towards solutions, and adaptable amidst uncertainty.
In this role, you will lead budgeting, forecasting, and financial planning; and oversee accounting, controls, and compliance. You’ll manage a small, highly collaborative team (including an Accounting Manager and a Finance Manager) and bring clear financial leadership to a complex, multi-entity nonprofit, working closely with Legal, Compliance, and organizational leadership. You’ll partner with Partnerships to deliver accurate, timely donor reporting. And ultimately, you will be the person colleagues consult to understand the financial implications of a decision, to weigh the risks and tradeoffs, and to assess alignment between resources and strategy.
About our organization: Protect Democracy formed in late 2016, recognizing that the global wave of authoritarianism had begun to erode American shores . We have since assembled a team of 120+ experts who have served under Democrats and Republicans and in the senior ranks of other nonprofit, political, or media organizations. Our team includes lawyers, policy experts, legislative advocates, media strategists, writers, data analysts, and software developers. In 2023, our team received a Skoll Award for Social Innovation and a MacArthur Fellowship . We anchor all of our work in service of our mission: it is the foundation of our team, be it litigation, advocacy, or ensuring that our organization has the secure financial operations to continue to meet the urgency of the moment.
You can work remotely from nearly any location in the United States.* We strongly encourage candidates from diverse backgrounds and from across the political and ideological spectrum to apply.A commitment to our mission and cross-ideological strategy for defending our democracy is essential.
The priority deadline to apply for this role is November 15, 2026; we will review applications received after that date on a rolling basis. Please note that candidates who reach the final hiring stage will be required to satisfactorily complete a pre-offer background check.**
The Director of Finance will:

• Lead organizational budgeting, forecasting, and financial planning , including annual budgets, multi-year projections, scenario analysis, and financial reporting, ensuring leadership has timely, accurate, and actionable information to support strategic decisions and resource allocation;

• Lead and integrate the Finance function , managing the Accounting Manager and Finance Manager, developing staff and managers, and establishing clear priorities, responsibilities, and sustainable workloads across accounting, finance operations, payroll, and related activities;

• Direct accounting, financial controls, and compliance , including month-end close, audits, tax filings, regulatory reporting, financial policies, and internal controls, ensuring accuracy, timely execution, and appropriate oversight of the organization's financial activities;

• Provide financial leadership across complex nonprofit structures , including multiple entities, state charitable registrations, grant funding, cost allocations, and other arrangements requiring sound financial judgment and coordination with Legal, Compliance, Partnerships, and organizational leadership;

• Serve as a trusted financial partner to executive leadership and teams across Protect Democracy , helping colleagues understand financial implications, evaluate risks and tradeoffs, and make informed decisions while establishing clear expectations for financial planning, forecasting, and cross-functional coordination;

• Lead improvements to financial systems, processes, and infrastructure , overseeing the effectiveness of contract-to-payment, procurement, payroll, and financial

At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

As Category Managers for Indirect Procurement, we develop strategic supplier relationships within our categories: Marketing and Distribution, Professional Services, Operations, Real Estate and Facilities Management, Bus, Infrastructure, and Fuel. We are looking for you to join our team and help us manage one or more of these categories.

About the Role

• Define and implement the (global) category strategy for one or more of these categories: Marketing &amp; Distribution and/or Operations

• Align the medium- and long-term category strategy with your business stakeholders and develop tailored sourcing strategies for individual projects within your categories

• Lead (global) tenders and sourcing projects, drive contract negotiations, and finalize agreements that deliver the best value while ensuring compliance with our Supplier Code of Conduct

• Build networks across the Flix Group to identify group-wide cost-reduction, optimization, and synergy potential

• Manage suppliers end to end, from selection and evaluation to development

• Conduct market analyses and RFI processes and optimize specifications to develop competitive sourcing alternative

About You

• Possess a bachelor's or master's degree in economics, business administration, or a comparable field

• Bring several years of relevant experience in category management, with in-depth knowledge of one or more of the categories listed above

• Have a proven track record of successful negotiations and category development

• Show a high degree of initiative and a strong drive for continuous improvement

• You are fluent in business German (native speaker preferred) and English

• Think and act entrepreneurially and have excellent communication skills

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

NB: Please submit your resume in English!

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

To view more local benefits specific to each office location, please check out this link:&nbsp; Locations - Flix Career

Why Join Flix?

At Flix, you’ll find teams that rally together to overcome challenges and spark creativity. We believe in ownership culture - giving you the freedom to take initiative, make an impact, and shape your own career path.
As we continue to expand across the globe, you can make a real difference in how we work.

If you’re ready to grow and lead your journey, Flix is the place for you!&nbsp;

